Good to know:API Routes do not specify CORS headers, meaning they are same-origin only by default.Since API Routes run on the server, we're able to use sensitive values (like API keys) through Environment Variables without exposing them to the client. This is critical for the security of your application.

We recommend using HTML validation like required and type="email" for basic client-side form validation.

